# Root .dockerignore
#
# The Keycloak image is built with the REPO ROOT as its build context
# (docker/Dockerfile.keycloak, `context: ..`). Without this file the whole
# repository — .git (~14 MB), .secrets/ (live production secrets), and
# frontend/node_modules + frontend/.next (~540 MB) — is transferred to the
# Docker daemon and persisted in its build cache.
#
# Only the Keycloak build uses this context (backend/ and frontend/ have their
# own .dockerignore files), so it is safe to be aggressive here.

# Version control and CI metadata
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.ai_infinite_backlog.md

# Secrets — never send these to the daemon
.secrets/
.env.prod
.env.local
.env.*.local
frontend/.env.local

# Dependencies and build outputs
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/target/
**/dist/
**/bin/
frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Local fixtures and scratch data
backend/.e2e-fixtures/
docs/
*.log
.DS_Store
